  "proof": [
    "477698 clears complete EAX before eight independent DWORD flag tests. A taken first test sets EAX=1; each of the remaining seven taken tests increments complete EAX once. No other path writes EAX.",
    "All256 Boolean test outcomes therefore return the sum in0..8 with native upper24 bits zero; the eight DWORD inputs remain arbitrary and use wrapped tile*4.",
    "Existing C unit01050 initializes a char from the first Boolean and adds the remaining seven Boolean tests. The char never exceeds8; its ordinary C result is exactly the same sum.",
    "4868F6 compares complete native EAX with8. The preserved C char API compares its actual logical0..8 value with8, so no missing high-register input or changed callee declaration is required.",
    "Parent ADD ESP8 then CMP EAX8 replaces arithmetic flags before any branch; native child flag residue is not consumed."
  ],
